## Advanced: Testing Complex Components (Multiple APIs & Contexts)

When testing advanced components (like Dashboards or Management Panels) that rely on both User Role context (`useAuth`) and multiple backend APIs, it's essential to reset your mocks and return specific values for each test case.

**Example for a Role-Based Component:**

```typescript
import { render, screen, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import * as api from '@/api/api';
import { useAuth } from '@/app/context/AuthContext';
import UserSpace from './UserSpace';

// 1. Mock the entire API module and the AuthContext
jest.mock('@/api/api', () => ({
  getUserEnrollments: jest.fn(),
  getAllUsers: jest.fn(),
}));

jest.mock('@/app/context/AuthContext', () => ({
  useAuth: jest.fn(),
}));

describe('UserSpace Component', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // 2. Clear previous states between tests
    jest.clearAllMocks();
  });

  test('renders user specific view', async () => {
    // 3. Mock the role to USER
    (useAuth as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue({
      isAuthenticated: true,
      role: 'USER',
    });

    // 4. Return user-specific data
    (api.getUserEnrollments as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([{ id: 1, courseTitle: 'React 101' }]);

    render(<UserSpace />);

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('React 101')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });

    // Ensure admin functionality is hidden
    expect(screen.queryByText('Admin Panel')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  test('renders admin specific view', async () => {
    // 3. Mock the role to ADMIN
    (useAuth as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue({
      isAuthenticated: true,
      role: 'ADMIN',
    });

    // 4. Return admin-specific data
    (api.getUserEnrollments as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([]);
    (api.getAllUsers as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([{ id: 1, nombre: 'Admin User' }]);

    render(<UserSpace />);

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('Admin Panel')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });
  });
});
```
